   "slug": "speech-825293",
   "speaker": "George Brandis",
   "party": "Liberal",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2013-06-27",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The Coalition supported the Crimes Legislation Amendment Bill 2013 as making sensible technical changes to investigations and prosecutions of people-smuggling crew, but strongly criticised the rushed 40-hour submission period that undermined public scrutiny and Senate committee processes. Specific provisions included removing wrist X-rays for age determination due to scientific concerns and placing the burden of proof on the prosecution to establish a person was an adult at the time of an offence."
  }
